---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Casey Key, the instructor behind Key Camp.">
  <article class="about wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The instructor</p>
    <h1>Technology should open more doors.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Casey Key. I’m a software engineer, systems architect, and educator. I’m building Key Camp so more young people can make useful things with AI.</p>

    <section class="about-grid">
      <div>
        <h2>Why I teach</h2>
        <p>I work at the intersection of AI, security, and large-scale systems. I also care about what happens after the technical work is done. I want to help create jobs, scholarships, and better opportunities for the people coming up behind me.</p>
        <p>I grew up low-income and Native American. I want Key Camp to reach rural Indigenous communities and inner-city youth because money and connections should not decide who gets to work with these tools.</p>
        <p>The project does not have to be about computer science. A student might build around art, construction, local history, music, entrepreneurship, a community need, or software. Their interests are the starting point.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="facts">
        <p class="eyebrow">Experience that informs the course</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Student instructor at the Northrop Grumman STEM Camp</li>
          <li>Teaching assistant for Python courses at Colorado State University</li>
          <li>Engineer across Oracle, AWS, Capital One, Amazon, and Salesforce</li>
          <li>MS in Computer Science student at Georgia Tech</li>
          <li>Builder of Spirit Beads, a store for a Native American artisan</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="principles">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I believe</p>
      <div class="principle-list"><p><strong>Give students working tools.</strong> A demo is not enough. They need to make something and see it work.</p><p><strong>Let students bring the context.</strong> The agent can implement. The student knows why the project matters.</p><p><strong>Start with their interests.</strong> Coding is one path. It is not the price of admission.</p></div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .wrap { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem; } .eyebrow { color: var(--lime); font: 500 .72rem 'DM Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; } h1 { max-width: 900px; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 8rem); line-height: .9; letter-spacing: -.08em; } h1 em { color: var(--orange); font-style: normal; } .lede { max-width: 700px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.35rem; } .about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(280px, .7fr); gap: 4rem; margin-top: 6rem; } h2 { font-size: 2.5rem; letter-spacing: -.05em; } p { color: var(--muted); } .facts { align-self: start; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); } ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; } li { margin: .8rem 0; color: var(--muted); } li::marker { color: var(--lime); } .principles { margin-top: 7rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } .principle-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem; } .principle-list p { padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); } .principle-list strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .5rem; color: var(--ink); } @media (max-width: 700px) { .wrap { padding-top: 2rem; } .about-grid, .principle-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 3rem; } h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 15vw, 6rem); } }
</style>
